WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.133
Welcome back.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.300
As you guys know, we're always striving to get better

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.634
here at "The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:09.200
♪ Harder, better, faster, stronger ♪

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.601
[ Laughter ] So, before every show,

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.601
we put out a suggestion box for the audience

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.200
just to get some feedback about what you guys think of the show,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.167
things you would like to us do, that kind of stuff.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.501
So tonight let's look inside the Audience Suggestion Box.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:21.801
Here we go.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:25.033
-♪ Look into the box, the suggestion box ♪

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.467
-This first one here is from Sheena Brooks.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.834
"Hey, Jimmy, I just went to see 'Beetlejuice: The Musical'

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.133
on Broadway, and it was amazing.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.667
I wish there were musical versions

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.534
of other Halloween movies. Can you help?"

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.801
Well, it's not really a Halloween movie, but they're

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.200
actually working on a musical reboot of "The Shining."

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.200
-Really? -Yeah, it looks pretty good.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.801
Here's a sneak peek.

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.501
♪♪

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:48.400
-♪ Little pigs, little pigs ♪

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.834
♪ Let me come in ♪

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.334
-♪ Ahh-ahh ♪

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:54.334
♪ Not by the hair on your chinny chin, chin! ♪

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.367
-♪ Ahh, ahh ♪ -♪ Ahh, ahh ♪

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.968
-♪ Don't ♪

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.200
♪ Jack, please, ahh ♪

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.634
-♪ I'll huff ♪ -♪ Ahh ♪

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.300
-♪ I'll puff ♪ -♪ Ahh ♪

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.834
♪ And I'll blow your house in ♪

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.400
-♪ Ahh ♪

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.133
-♪ Here's Johnny! ♪

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.000
-Wow.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:21.133
♪♪

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.968
-Wow! -Wow. Scary, huh?

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.100
-I'm gonna go see that. -Scary.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.934
Let's try another one. This is from Emmy Dyer.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.200
"Hey, Jimmy, do you think you can toss an apple-cider donut

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.234
and have it land on Higgins' head?"

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.634
That's a good question. There's only one way to find out.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.734
You ready, Higgins?

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.167
-Yep.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.200
-It goes like this way or...? -Like that way. Yeah.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.601
-Toss it like that? -There you go.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.834
-Like that way? -You got it.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.567
-Or that way? -That way.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:46.200
I would say like a frisbee.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.534
[ Pop! ]

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:54.200
-[ Chuckles ] Not bad.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.234
Don't forget the hole, Joel!

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:57.501
[ Pop! ]

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:58.868
There you go.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.701
This is from Randy McStine.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:07.100
"Hey, Jimmy, the FIFA World Cup is coming up, and I can't wait.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.100
My favorite thing about the game is when the guy yells,

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.634
'G-o-o-o-ol' after someone scores.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:15.234
I wonder what it would sound like if he yelled 'Lizzo.'"

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.100
Well, we can make that happen right now.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.667
Ladies and gentlemen, please welcome the legend himself,

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.367
Andrés Cantor, a.k.a. "Mr. Gol,"

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.234
saying the word "Lizzo."

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:44.834
-Lizz-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o!

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:50.667
-That's what I'm talking about! Andrés Cantor!

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.067
Andrés, thank you, buddy.

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.634
Legend. Legend.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.133
Alright. We'll do one last one here.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.901
-Alright. Great.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.267
-Alright. Here we go. We'll do one last one here.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.801
It's from Sarah Munson.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.567
"Hey, Jimmy, I'm a big fan of Ford trucks,

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:06.801
and I especially love

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:09.100
their all-new F-Series Super Duty pickup truck."

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.868
It's awesome. Work hard, play hard.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:15.267
The problem is, I love trivia games that involve a giant pie

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.634
made of whipped cream being launched

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.067
at someone from a catapult.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:20.801
Is there any way you can combine those things?"

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:24.334
Well, Sarah, you're in luck because...

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.601
[ Laughter ] -Wow.

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:29.834
-There's a Ford Super Duty down in the 30 Rock Plaza

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.400
with a catapult attached to it

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.267
that can launch a giant whipped cream pie through the air.

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.534
Let's do this!

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.267
Wanna do this? Come on, Higg. Come on, Tariq.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:40.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:46.834
♪♪

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:52.734
♪♪

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.267
Hey, guys, we're down in the 30 Rock Plaza.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:58.734
Tariq and I are about to play the Ford Mega Pie Challenge.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:01.801
Higgins, tell us how it works. -Well, the game is simple.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.868
In front of you is a Ford Super Duty

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.868
equipped with a whipped-cream catapult.

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.634
You'll answer trivia questions

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.834
designed to test your knowledge about the Super Duty.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.901
If you guess right, you move on.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:16.701
If you guess wrong, you must press the cream launcher,

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:20.000
which will randomly trigger the giant pie to be thrown at you.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.267
Alright. Here's your first question.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:44.367
-I'm a pumpkin hauler myself.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.534
Pumpkins average around 4 pounds per pumpkin.

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.200
-Oh, my God. -I'm gonna say my answer is B.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.234
-B. That is correct!

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.834
10,000 pumpkins.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:56.234
Tariq, it's your turn in the cream zone.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:58.100
And here's your question.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.534
-I'm gonna say "A." I'm gonna say "A."

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:19.667
-"A."

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:20.901
[ Buzzer ] Ooh, sorry.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.067
"C, 360 degrees.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.601
-Oh, great.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.133
You must now press the cream launcher.

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.601
-Yeah! Come on! -Which may or may not

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:34.334
trigger the pie to be catapulted unto you.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.767
Good luck. -Good luck, bud.

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:38.567
[ Suspenseful music ]

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:44.334
♪♪

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.701
[ Ding ]

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:47.667
-Ohh. -Whew!

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.567
-Unbelievable. -Jimmy -- You survived, Tariq.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.234
Jimmy, you're up. Your question is...

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:14.834
-So does the truck have the torque of a truck?

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:17.067
-Does it? That's up to you.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:19.667
-Trying to trick me, but sure. -You're gonna go "A"?

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:20.868
-Yeah.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:21.868
[ Buzzer ] -Ooh. Wrong!

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:23.601
It is "B," a semi truck.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.767
Jimmy, press the cream launcher.

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:26.901
Good luck!

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.834
[ Suspenseful music ]

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:36.367
♪♪

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:37.434
[ Ding ]

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.601
Ohh! You survived.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:42.667
Tariq, you're up. -Unh!

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.300
-I'm gonna go "D," all of the above.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.734
-This is insane. -That is correct! "D." Yes!

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:07.334
Alright, Jimmy, your question. -I know.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.100
-Is it, "A," eggs and toast...

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.834
"B," cereal...

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:21.701
"C," steel-cut oatmeal...

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:24.000
or, "D," a raspberry pain au chocolat

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.634
with a quiche Lorraine and a warm hazelnut ganache

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:28.667
with a hint of cinnamon? -Hint of cinnamon.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:31.167
-I am definitely going -- I've been to breakfast with you.

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:32.467
It is "D."

00:07:32.467 --> 00:07:34.000
[ Buzzer ] -Oh, no!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.167
Of course, it's "C," steel-cut oatmeal.

00:07:36.167 --> 00:07:38.534
Come on, man! Time to press it, baby.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.400
Press the launcher. -Moment of truth.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.367
[ Suspenseful music ]

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:45.033
♪♪

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:46.701
[ Engine revs ]

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:51.767
♪♪

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:54.300
[ Mozart's "Requiem in D Minor" plays ]

00:07:54.300 --> 00:08:04.300
♪♪

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:14.234
♪♪

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:16.267
[ Applause ]

00:08:16.267 --> 00:08:22.901
♪♪

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:24.601
-Ohh!

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:31.300
-That's all the time we have for Suggestion Box.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.367
Thank you so much to Ford. Really, thank you, Ford.

00:08:34.367 --> 00:08:36.567
We'll be right back with more "Tonight Show," everybody.

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:37.801
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:39.701
-♪ ...my favorite cartoon ♪

00:08:39.701 --> 00:08:41.634
♪ After that, there's a honeymoon ♪

